IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-supply`

-- Electricity Act 2001, my supply and my premises, from the occupier's seat -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_electricity-act-2001_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a household short of income, no offer of advice yet` MEANS `My unpaid account` WITH
    `I am a contestable consumer` IS FALSE
    `the premises are residential` IS TRUE
    `I failed to pay through lack of sufficient income of my household` IS TRUE
    `the licensee offered to advise me about optional methods of arranging payment` IS FALSE
    `the period the licensee gave me, in days` IS 0
    `I did not accept the offer of advice within that period` IS FALSE
    `I accepted the advice but took no reasonable action to pay within that period` IS FALSE
    `the period has run` IS FALSE
    `the unpaid charges are due to a transmission licensee` IS FALSE

`a household short of income that let a 7-day offer of advice lapse` MEANS `My unpaid account` WITH
